# Build context for dashboard/deploy/Dockerfile, which is built FROM THE REPO
# ROOT because the image carries four trees that live in four different
# directories (dashboard/, broll/web, music/web, ytdl/web):
#
#   docker build -f dashboard/deploy/Dockerfile -t ccsync-dashboard:<ver> .
#
# The repo is ~2 GB and all but ~10 MB of that is data and build output the
# image must never contain. A denylist rather than the `*` + `!path` allowlist
# form on purpose: the four trees are named in the Dockerfile's COPY lines, so
# an allowlist here would state the same fact twice and go stale silently
# (2026-08-17, COMMERCIAL_READINESS.md item 12).

.git
.github
.pytest_cache
.cache
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.pyc
**/.venv

# Components that are not in the container at all. Together ~350 MB, most of
# it PyInstaller dist/ and build/ output.
companion
onboarding
bench
installer
tools
server
docs
# ...EXCEPT the MARKDOWN under it, which is what the running dashboard serves
# (REL-5, usability sweep 2026-09-04; widened from two documents to the tree
# the same day, at the owner's request): the licence agreement the first-run
# wizard makes an admin accept, and every document /help browses. ~4 MB of
# text. Without it an image-mode container shows an empty licence box with a
# disabled [ ACCEPT ], ticks the wizard's `eula` task green, and says help is
# not installed.
#
# `*.md` and nothing else on purpose: docs/mobile alone is a directory of
# screenshots, and an image is not made of documentation. Both patterns are
# needed - `**` matches zero directories here, but stating the top level
# explicitly is cheaper than trusting that. A re-inclusion has to come AFTER
# the directory that excludes it: the last matching pattern wins.
!docs/*.md
!docs/**/*.md
broll/indexer
music/indexer

# Test suites and their fixtures: excluded from the SHIPPED trees for the same
# reason install_dashboard_app.py's BROLL_EXCLUDE_DIRS excludes them -- they
# are not runtime code and some carry fixture media.
**/tests
**/node_modules

# The data roots. music/web/data alone is 1.5 GB (music.db + the exported CLAP
# text encoder), and every one of these is a MOUNT at runtime, never image
# content: /broll-data, /music-data, /music-encoder, /ytdl-data.
broll/web/data
music/web/data
ytdl/web/data

# Site identity and secrets. site.toml names one customer's NAS; it reaches
# the container through the environment (compose), never baked into a layer.
site.toml
site.example.toml
*.log
